## Questionnaires and packs
    
    - Upload a questionnaire from Evidence (check “Treat as questionnaire”) or use the demo PQQ.
    - Create a response pack. Status is computed: GREEN / AMBER / RED / EXPIRED / CONFLICT.
    - Approving wording does not change evidence status. Exports keep that status.
    - Export JSON / XLSX / DOCX. Re-open the file. GREEN rows must cite live facts.
    
    ## Export, leave, delete
    
    - Admins can download an **organisation snapshot** (metadata, members, facts, answers). File bytes and live invite codes are omitted.
    - Any member except the last owner can **leave**.
    - Owners can **delete** the organisation by typing its exact name. This wipes memberships, evidence, facts, packs, exports, jobs, and audit.
    
    ## Roles
    
    | Role | Can |
    |---|---|
    | viewer | read, download originals |
    | contributor | upload, extract, create packs |
    | reviewer | approve facts/answers, export, invalidate sources |
    | admin | manage members, load demo, snapshot |
    | owner | all of the above, including delete organisation |
    
    ## Limits
    
    - 10 organisations created / user / hour
    - 60 uploads / user / hour
    - 60 invites / user / org / hour
    - 30 AI extracts / user / org / hour
    - 25 memberships / user
    - 5,000 documents / org (including archived)
    - 250 live pending invites / org
    - 500 packs / org
    - 2,000 stored exports / org
    
    429 responses say how many seconds to wait.
    
    ## What this product does not do
    
    No mailer, SAML, OCR, FX conversion, or background worker. Invitations are capability codes shown in the UI. Set `WALLET_SIGNUP_OPEN=false` to reject new email/password **and** new Grok broker OAuth accounts (existing users still sign in). The landing/login/signup UI stays unknown until `/ready` answers 200 with `signupOpen: true`, and fail-closed on a non-OK or failed fetch. Unverified email/password can occupy a mailbox while signup is open (accepted risk K23). There is no password-reset email.
    
